ter hard knocks  I think they're looking great I'm  excited about all the new weapons they  got on offense I think the Tyrod Taylor  Baker dynamic has really been great so  far and I expect that to continue  anything tyrunt's the perfect guy to  help mentor but also still be the leader  and be the guy that's behind the center  so that's exciting I mean I'm I'm  anxiously waiting for Josh Gordon to  come back and see how that changes the  office but I think even if he's not back  anytime soon I think they can really  score a lot of points on office this  year if you were still playing offensive  tackle for the Browns who would you want  to start week one as your quarterback  I've always said this that I think  experience is underrated at the  quarterback position so I would  definitely go with Tyrod I think I  played with a lot of rookie quarterbacks  and a lot of times they look great in  practice they look great in the  preseason but once you start throwing  stuff at them that they haven't been  coached up that week they have a hard  time and I think playing quarterback a  lot of times what happens during the  course of a season as you're falling  back on some of the experiences that  you've had early on in your career  whether it be defensive coverages or  blitz packages or how you're going to  handle certain blitz pickups and if you  don't have those experiences to fall  back on a lot of times that's when big  negative plays happen and that's what  you see a lot from rookie quarterbacks  how often did you go into a game  actually thinking you could win well to  be totally honest in later on in my  career as the losing sort of piled up I  didn't really even think about that I  just kind of focused on my job and  trying to win my individual battle and I  just focused on how can I be perfect in  this game and give my team the best  chance to win because I didn't want to  think like a fan because I knew that  would lead to a decrease in my own  performance because I 